1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,220
Cheers!

2
00:00:44,120 --> 00:00:47,117
Men like him can't help
themselves from dreaming.

3
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:51,257
He gazes towards tomorrow,
eyes are gleaming.

4
00:00:51,340 --> 00:00:55,137
But every day a dreamer
fights against reality.

5
00:00:55,220 --> 00:00:59,140
It seems a struggle to be free.

6
00:01:00,760 --> 00:01:03,460
If I were alone, I might surrender.

7
00:01:05,120 --> 00:01:07,900
Weight's too heavy for me.

8
00:01:08,880 --> 00:01:13,200
When I hear him say it,
even I can't believe.

9
00:01:16,440 --> 00:01:20,317
Today is the day, we'll
bury all our sorrow.

10
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:22,477
Time to raise the sails,
they'll tell our tales.

11
00:01:22,560 --> 00:01:24,137
Through every tomorrow.

12
00:01:24,220 --> 00:01:28,437
Today is the day, we're
aiming towards a new dawn.

13
00:01:28,520 --> 00:01:29,477
And all our doubts are gone.

14
00:01:29,560 --> 00:01:30,457
Let's move along.

15
00:01:30,540 --> 00:01:33,200
Cause it's time to sail away.

16
00:01:35,520 --> 00:01:38,440
For the new world.

17
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:42,400
For the new world.

18
00:01:43,260 --> 00:01:46,017
For the new world.

19
00:01:46,100 --> 00:01:49,400
Where our dreams will all come true.

20
00:01:56,480 --> 00:01:58,660
Oh, so long.

21
00:02:15,140 --> 00:02:16,320
What the?

22
00:02:16,860 --> 00:02:17,690
Huh?

23
00:02:23,540 --> 00:02:24,460
Bunch of fools!

24
00:02:24,800 --> 00:02:27,177
Why did you have to get
all sentimental like that?

25
00:02:27,260 --> 00:02:29,319
Now we can't cash it on his bounty!

26
00:02:31,760 --> 00:02:35,197
If you don't get out of our way,
we'll arrest every last one of you!

27
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:36,557
I'd like to see you try.

28
00:02:36,640 --> 00:02:39,117
Just let the man play his
rock and roll, damn it!

29
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:41,082
Hey, what's going on over there?

30
00:02:41,280 --> 00:02:43,057
It's out of control,
I'll tell you that much!

31
00:02:43,140 --> 00:02:47,117
The Navy came to arrest Soul King during
his show when I was there to rioting!

32
00:02:47,200 --> 00:02:49,435
Looks like he made his escape, though.

33
00:02:50,620 --> 00:02:51,855
You skinless traitor!

34
00:02:52,100 --> 00:02:53,453
I'm gonna make you pay!

35
00:02:54,620 --> 00:02:56,577
Anyway, that's not the big story here.

36
00:02:56,660 --> 00:02:59,457
Soul King is actually a pirate
known as the Humming Swordsman.

37
00:02:59,540 --> 00:03:01,240
He's one of the Straw Hats!

38
00:03:07,260 --> 00:03:09,237
Thank you for the ride, my friend.

39
00:03:09,320 --> 00:03:11,849
And that was impeccable
timing, I must say.

40
00:03:11,940 --> 00:03:13,997
You can thank Chaka for
putting all this together.

41
00:03:14,080 --> 00:03:15,877
Your friends should be
waiting for you at Grove 42.

42
00:03:15,960 --> 00:03:18,897
I'm so eager to see them
again my heart is beating out

43
00:03:18,980 --> 00:03:22,680
of my chest kidding obviously
my chest is an empty void.

44
00:03:28,320 --> 00:03:29,877
So here's the skinny brother?

45
00:03:29,960 --> 00:03:31,457
Luffy's on the island.

46
00:03:31,540 --> 00:03:34,797
Somewhere but the Navy's
about to close in and the

47
00:03:34,880 --> 00:03:37,797
rest of the crew is headed
to grove 42 meet us there!

48
00:03:37,880 --> 00:03:39,100
Roger that Franky.

49
00:03:39,760 --> 00:03:42,417
What's up great you mean
you weren't listening?

50
00:03:42,500 --> 00:03:43,880
Well, let's see

51
00:03:45,400 --> 00:03:46,740
Navy, come here.

52
00:03:47,040 --> 00:03:48,860
Us pirates, ship.

53
00:03:49,280 --> 00:03:50,280
Run away.

54
00:03:50,620 --> 00:03:51,940
Is that clear enough?

55
00:03:52,120 --> 00:03:53,517
Why are you talking like that?

56
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:55,659
Did you hit your head or something?

57
00:03:56,080 --> 00:03:56,910
Sorry.

58
00:03:56,993 --> 00:04:00,000
I just thought I'd speak on
your level for once. Huh?

59
00:04:00,500 --> 00:04:01,441
All right, then.

60
00:04:01,940 --> 00:04:04,440
After this, stupid cook, die.

61
00:04:05,140 --> 00:04:06,060
Real funny.

62
00:04:06,440 --> 00:04:08,937
Anyway, you know what all that
racket over there is about?

63
00:04:09,020 --> 00:04:09,850
Huh?

64
00:04:11,660 --> 00:04:12,900
You, right.

65
00:04:22,940 --> 00:04:25,620
All right, that's enough yakking. Listen!

66
00:04:27,200 --> 00:04:30,920
Turns out Sanji and Zoro found
one of the guys who insulted me.

67
00:04:31,520 --> 00:04:33,696
In fact, he's here with us right now.

68
00:04:34,740 --> 00:04:36,460
Look at this little punk.

69
00:04:36,900 --> 00:04:40,057
I'm gonna beat a lesson into
him with my own two hands.

70
00:04:40,140 --> 00:04:43,460
Because when you piss me
off, then things get ugly.

71
00:04:44,160 --> 00:04:46,900
And let this be a lesson
to all of you, too.

72
00:04:47,220 --> 00:04:50,700
If you ever cross me, if
you ever disrespect me,

73
00:04:50,800 --> 00:04:52,757
you're going to end up
just like this chump.

74
00:04:52,840 --> 00:04:55,157
Don't forget who's the boss of this crew.

75
00:04:55,240 --> 00:04:56,652
Is that perfectly clear?

76
00:04:58,280 --> 00:05:01,937
You're in that bounty somehow, and
it wasn't by playing News Nights.

77
00:05:02,020 --> 00:05:05,000
What's with this guy? Zoro? Sanji?

78
00:05:05,160 --> 00:05:06,837
A friend of yours or something?

79
00:05:06,920 --> 00:05:08,520
I don't think he likes me.

80
00:05:09,520 --> 00:05:10,991
We've got you surrounded.

81
00:05:11,100 --> 00:05:12,340
Nobody move an inch.

82
00:05:12,820 --> 00:05:16,197
Straw Hat Luffy, you and the rest
of your crew are under arrest.

83
00:05:16,280 --> 00:05:18,460
Surrender immediately. The Navy?

84
00:05:18,880 --> 00:05:20,277
And don't bother running away.

85
00:05:20,360 --> 00:05:22,595
We blocked off every exit in Grove 46.

86
00:05:22,840 --> 00:05:25,117
You guys leave with us or you're
going to leave in a body bag.

87
00:05:25,200 --> 00:05:26,680
My disguise is perfect.

88
00:05:26,800 --> 00:05:28,741
How did the Navy know I was here?

89
00:05:28,920 --> 00:05:31,237
Why would you think
that this was about you?

90
00:05:31,320 --> 00:05:33,497
Captain, please tell
me we're not all dead.

91
00:05:33,580 --> 00:05:34,417
Stop flipping out.

92
00:05:34,500 --> 00:05:35,357
We'll be just fine.

93
00:05:35,440 --> 00:05:37,397
Why do you think we
recruited all these guys?

94
00:05:37,480 --> 00:05:41,077
We've got pirates with hundred million
bounties here, but this is scary!

95
00:05:41,160 --> 00:05:42,800
Then sit back and watch.

96
00:05:44,560 --> 00:05:48,857
Caribou Europe use that marine as a shield
and make us a path out of this dump?

97
00:05:48,940 --> 00:05:51,877
Wait what marine we sent
a scout here earlier

98
00:05:51,960 --> 00:05:54,557
that looks like he was
taken captive damn it.

99
00:05:54,640 --> 00:05:55,522
That's not good

100
00:06:01,320 --> 00:06:03,677
Although that would be
terribly convenient.

101
00:06:03,760 --> 00:06:05,525
I'm afraid it simply won't do!

102
00:06:06,020 --> 00:06:06,850
Why not?

103
00:06:06,933 --> 00:06:09,657
Because he told me he
hadn't called the Navy yet.

104
00:06:09,740 --> 00:06:12,093
And that makes him a filthy little liar.

105
00:06:15,040 --> 00:06:15,880
Caribou, no!

106
00:06:24,620 --> 00:06:26,340
That crazy bastard!

107
00:06:26,620 --> 00:06:28,502
Who's the captain here, damn it?

108
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:31,200
Oh, well, so much for that plan.

109
00:06:31,960 --> 00:06:34,537
You high and mighty type
seem to think it's all right

110
00:06:34,620 --> 00:06:37,397
to lie to someone if
they're a so-called bad guy.

111
00:06:37,480 --> 00:06:38,833
Well, I object to that.

112
00:06:40,960 --> 00:06:42,877
I guess they're not surrendering, huh?

113
00:06:42,960 --> 00:06:44,607
Should have figured as much.

114
00:06:44,760 --> 00:06:46,760
George, show the pirates no mercy!

115
00:06:48,600 --> 00:06:49,430
Good luck!

116
00:06:49,560 --> 00:06:51,197
Our boss is Straw Hat Luffy.

117
00:06:51,280 --> 00:06:53,397
He's not going to lose to
a bunch of chumps like you.

118
00:06:53,480 --> 00:06:54,310
Let's go!

119
00:06:58,540 --> 00:07:00,337
If you've got a plan, I'd hurry!

120
00:07:00,420 --> 00:07:03,197
Listen to your captain, you
guys are pissing me off!

121
00:07:03,280 --> 00:07:07,077
That guy just said that I was his boss,
but I've never even seen him before.

122
00:07:07,160 --> 00:07:10,454
I do not have time to deal
with your nonsense right now.

123
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:22,980
Aim for the captain in charge!

124
00:07:24,860 --> 00:07:25,960
I know you.

125
00:07:26,540 --> 00:07:27,980
You're lip service Daddy.

126
00:07:28,300 --> 00:07:30,280
Your bounty's 88 million.

127
00:07:31,880 --> 00:07:34,757
You may be idiots, but at
least you're not cowards.

128
00:07:34,840 --> 00:07:36,546
Don't let him intimidate you!

129
00:07:41,140 --> 00:07:42,060
Holy crap!

130
00:07:42,360 --> 00:07:44,242
He's got a bounty of 92 million!

131
00:07:44,840 --> 00:07:46,380
That's gashed Albion!

132
00:07:48,960 --> 00:07:50,180
We'll take him down!

133
00:07:50,480 --> 00:07:52,120
Justice is on our side!

134
00:07:54,340 --> 00:07:57,057
The ground is soaked with
the blood of hypocrites.

135
00:07:57,140 --> 00:07:59,217
Its overwhelming stench makes me so sick.

136
00:07:59,300 --> 00:08:05,320
A 210 million bounty, wet-haired
caribou, too late to surrender now!

137
00:08:06,460 --> 00:08:09,520
Oh, damn it, no one said
he had a Devil Fruit power!

138
00:08:10,760 --> 00:08:12,960
Why don't we all slow down a bit?

139
00:08:13,360 --> 00:08:16,713
Haven't you heard that stress
can lead to an early grave?

140
00:08:18,100 --> 00:08:19,160
My sword!

141
00:08:22,940 --> 00:08:23,770
What?

142
00:08:25,040 --> 00:08:26,120
Pass-a-bistas!

143
00:08:26,940 --> 00:08:27,770
Oh, hell.

144
00:08:34,620 --> 00:08:37,091
Nobody told me they were going to be here.

145
00:08:38,640 --> 00:08:40,857
I kind of want to beat
up those robot guys,

146
00:08:40,940 --> 00:08:43,817
but Hancock said to stay out
of trouble, so I guess I won't.

147
00:08:43,900 --> 00:08:48,194
Those things that vaporize the mustache
off your stupid face, you nutbag!

148
00:08:53,380 --> 00:08:54,210
Monkey D.

149
00:08:54,293 --> 00:08:55,689
Luffy has been identified.

150
00:08:55,820 --> 00:08:56,677
Commence attack.

151
00:08:56,760 --> 00:08:58,577
Those things are aiming straight at me.

152
00:08:58,660 --> 00:09:00,960
Can I even run or am I just dead?

153
00:09:01,860 --> 00:09:04,742
I was hoping I'd get to
rumble with them someday.

154
00:09:10,240 --> 00:09:13,380
Lip service, Daddy,
identified and subdued.

155
00:09:13,640 --> 00:09:14,758
Sustains no damage.

156
00:09:14,900 --> 00:09:16,157
Searching for next target.

157
00:09:16,240 --> 00:09:17,640
Captain Daddy!

158
00:09:20,560 --> 00:09:21,980
Follow the pacifistas!

159
00:09:22,240 --> 00:09:24,240
Capture every pirate in your path!

160
00:09:25,280 --> 00:09:26,317
Dodie's that cold.

161
00:09:26,400 --> 00:09:29,557
A bounty like that, and these guys
took him down in only one shot?

162
00:09:29,640 --> 00:09:30,470
We're screwed.

163
00:09:30,860 --> 00:09:32,180
Hang up, wait for us!

164
00:09:34,300 --> 00:09:35,920
I ain't waiting for nobody!

165
00:09:36,140 --> 00:09:37,497
The thing took out Daddy!

166
00:09:37,580 --> 00:09:38,933
I don't see the chance!

167
00:09:43,860 --> 00:09:45,157
Straw Hat, do something!

168
00:09:45,240 --> 00:09:47,652
You're the only one who can stop him now!

169
00:09:47,920 --> 00:09:51,997
I hate to beg, Captain, but your whole
crew is about to get blown up over here!

170
00:09:52,080 --> 00:09:53,727
There's no more left to run!

171
00:09:55,600 --> 00:09:57,337
Oh crap he's gone.

172
00:09:57,420 --> 00:09:58,720
Where is Straw Hat?

173
00:09:59,560 --> 00:10:02,317
They keep calling for their captain! But.

174
00:10:02,400 --> 00:10:04,937
My side is killing me.

175
00:10:05,020 --> 00:10:07,080
The lasers are gonna kill you!

176
00:10:08,380 --> 00:10:09,817
Get your fat ass!

177
00:10:09,900 --> 00:10:10,737
Out of my way!

178
00:10:10,820 --> 00:10:12,820
Who is this idiot?

179
00:10:16,600 --> 00:10:17,600
He's here.

180
00:10:18,620 --> 00:10:19,900
Captain Luffy!

181
00:10:24,400 --> 00:10:27,177
Am I mistaken or did they
call you Captain Luffy?

182
00:10:27,260 --> 00:10:28,837
Why wouldn't they call me that?

183
00:10:28,920 --> 00:10:29,750
I mean, you realize...

184
00:10:29,833 --> 00:10:31,237
Who you're talking to
right now, don't you?

185
00:10:31,320 --> 00:10:35,097
Go get out of my way before I grab
your intestines and pull them out!

186
00:10:35,180 --> 00:10:36,010
Your ear!

187
00:10:36,093 --> 00:10:37,177
I'd run if I were you!

188
00:10:37,260 --> 00:10:39,277
You're face to face
with the son of dragon!

189
00:10:39,360 --> 00:10:40,190
The revolutionary!

190
00:10:40,273 --> 00:10:43,577
That means I'm the
grandson of the hero! Garb!

191
00:10:43,660 --> 00:10:44,797
Oh and my bounty!

192
00:10:44,880 --> 00:10:48,120
It clucks into 400 million berries!

193
00:10:51,500 --> 00:10:52,777
Turn on Straw Hat!

194
00:10:52,860 --> 00:10:54,157
You human pile of garbage!

195
00:10:54,240 --> 00:10:55,440
Not even close!

196
00:11:03,520 --> 00:11:06,560
That guy just took out Straw Hat!

197
00:11:07,920 --> 00:11:09,057
So that's it!

198
00:11:09,140 --> 00:11:10,057
Fools!

199
00:11:10,140 --> 00:11:14,257
They thought that they could join the
Straw Hats and enter the New World!

200
00:11:14,340 --> 00:11:15,170
PX5!

201
00:11:15,253 --> 00:11:16,240
Who is this imposter?

202
00:11:20,660 --> 00:11:21,490
Confirmed.

203
00:11:21,573 --> 00:11:25,960
He is triple-tongued D 'Amato Black, a
pirate with a 26 million Barry Bounty.

204
00:11:26,620 --> 00:11:27,450
What?

205
00:11:27,533 --> 00:11:28,917
He's only worth 26 million.

206
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:29,940
That means...

207
00:11:30,780 --> 00:11:31,680
He's afraid!

208
00:11:34,600 --> 00:11:36,520
Look at guys, the jig is up!

209
00:11:37,420 --> 00:11:39,377
What the hell are we supposed to do now?

210
00:11:39,460 --> 00:11:43,477
It's bad enough this guy tricked us, but
now we got the Navy called on us too!

211
00:11:43,560 --> 00:11:45,637
Guess the real Straw
Hat is dead after all.

212
00:11:45,720 --> 00:11:46,840
What the hell?

213
00:11:47,080 --> 00:11:49,337
You mean Straw Hat
didn't get fat and gross?

214
00:11:49,420 --> 00:11:52,126
This guy was just fat
and gross to begin with?

215
00:11:52,580 --> 00:11:53,410
Wait, what?

216
00:11:53,493 --> 00:11:55,709
That fat gross guy was
pretending to be me?

217
00:11:55,940 --> 00:11:57,220
And Sanji and Zoro?

218
00:11:57,500 --> 00:12:00,441
They looked real, but I
guess they were fakes too.

219
00:12:00,820 --> 00:12:02,600
Wow, this is blowing my mind.

220
00:12:02,720 --> 00:12:04,117
I gotta get out of here.

221
00:12:04,200 --> 00:12:06,197
I know you aren't real Straw Hats,

222
00:12:06,280 --> 00:12:09,257
and you're just victims of this
fool, but you're still pirates.

223
00:12:09,340 --> 00:12:11,869
That means a lot of
you are coming with us.

224
00:12:13,800 --> 00:12:18,600
And although I cannot imagine why, the
real Straw Hat is here somewhere, too.

225
00:12:19,120 --> 00:12:23,840
When we entered the area, Pucci detected
him on the stage with the impostors.

226
00:12:24,240 --> 00:12:26,780
Fire on Straw Hat, Pucci!

227
00:12:36,920 --> 00:12:38,720
That was close!

228
00:12:41,520 --> 00:12:43,560
You almost blew up all my lunches!

229
00:12:43,700 --> 00:12:45,406
What did food ever do to you?

230
00:12:46,200 --> 00:12:48,497
Uh... Huh? Oof! It's...

231
00:12:48,580 --> 00:12:50,480
It's really him, isn't it?

232
00:12:55,400 --> 00:12:57,320
That's Straw Hat Loopy!

233
00:13:00,680 --> 00:13:03,860
The real Straw Hat was here
and we didn't even know!

234
00:13:04,220 --> 00:13:05,397
Nothing has changed, man!

235
00:13:05,480 --> 00:13:08,237
We came here to capture Straw
Hat and that's what we're doing!

236
00:13:08,320 --> 00:13:09,150
Sir!

237
00:13:09,233 --> 00:13:10,500
So there you are!

238
00:13:11,080 --> 00:13:13,668
I had enough of you the
last time we fought.

239
00:13:13,980 --> 00:13:15,740
I'm just trying to set sail.

240
00:13:15,920 --> 00:13:17,717
I'm not supposed to start any trouble.

241
00:13:17,800 --> 00:13:21,040
Oh, it's no trouble, but
you won't be setting sail.

242
00:13:21,320 --> 00:13:24,740
Unlike two years ago, I'm an
official Navy officer now.

243
00:13:24,940 --> 00:13:28,293
That means I'm taking you in
if it's the last thing I do.

244
00:13:28,420 --> 00:13:29,660
Pucci, fire!

245
00:13:37,100 --> 00:13:38,560
Is that all?

246
00:13:42,380 --> 00:13:43,500
What?

247
00:13:48,740 --> 00:13:50,480
Second gear!

248
00:13:56,360 --> 00:13:58,560
You're way too slow!

249
00:14:07,500 --> 00:14:09,640
Come, come, jet-pasta!

250
00:14:17,220 --> 00:14:19,020
This is worse than I thought.

251
00:14:19,460 --> 00:14:21,100
He can use Haki now.

252
00:14:24,700 --> 00:14:28,300
He made a passive beast up
and all it took was one horse.

253
00:14:36,220 --> 00:14:37,300
So long.

254
00:14:37,840 --> 00:14:40,917
So I have a feeling I'm gonna
see you again somewhere.

255
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:42,537
Get back here and fight me!

256
00:14:42,620 --> 00:14:43,617
Don't let him go, man!

257
00:14:43,700 --> 00:14:44,530
Hurry!

258
00:14:44,613 --> 00:14:45,443
Yes, sir!

259
00:14:49,980 --> 00:14:52,440
Hey! Luffy! Luffy! Should've known!

260
00:14:52,640 --> 00:14:56,522
All I had to do was follow the
explosions and I knew I'd find you!

261
00:14:58,340 --> 00:15:00,300
Okay, do for real this time!

262
00:15:00,580 --> 00:15:02,760
And Zora's not even fat! Way to go!

263
00:15:03,740 --> 00:15:05,060
Roronoa and Blackfoot!

264
00:15:05,300 --> 00:15:06,837
I should've known they were still alive!

265
00:15:06,920 --> 00:15:07,750
R .I .P.

266
00:15:07,833 --> 00:15:08,800
on summon attack!

267
00:15:17,600 --> 00:15:18,720
Get lost!

268
00:15:24,340 --> 00:15:26,720
I'm the one who got him. Keep dreaming!

269
00:15:26,940 --> 00:15:28,293
My kick broke his neck!

270
00:15:30,140 --> 00:15:32,740
It's the real Strawheads!
They're monsters!

271
00:15:33,200 --> 00:15:35,729
The big ones were
nothing like this at all!

272
00:15:41,560 --> 00:15:43,737
By the way, Luffy, you're number nine.

273
00:15:43,820 --> 00:15:44,650
Nobody cares!

274
00:15:44,733 --> 00:15:45,917
Would you give up on that?

275
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:47,377
Everyone's waiting at the sunny.

276
00:15:47,460 --> 00:15:48,460
Let's get moving.

277
00:15:48,660 --> 00:15:49,490
Got it!

278
00:15:51,020 --> 00:15:52,757
We're not missing this chance!

279
00:15:52,840 --> 00:15:53,877
Every last Marine!

280
00:15:53,960 --> 00:15:54,790
After them!

281
00:15:55,700 --> 00:15:57,460
Man, it's been forever, huh?

282
00:15:57,780 --> 00:15:59,900
I bet everyone's so cool now.

283
00:16:00,060 --> 00:16:01,560
I can't wait to see!

284
00:16:09,400 --> 00:16:10,840
What happened? Let's go!

285
00:16:20,800 --> 00:16:22,020
It can't be!

286
00:16:23,260 --> 00:16:24,789
That's Star King's really!

287
00:16:28,680 --> 00:16:32,504
I came to check on you, but it
seems you have this under control.

288
00:16:33,180 --> 00:16:36,180
In fact, you're even stronger
than when I left you.

289
00:16:37,660 --> 00:16:39,601
Finally time to see your friends.

290
00:16:39,760 --> 00:16:41,878
You've been waiting for long enough.

291
00:16:42,420 --> 00:16:44,360
Thanks, really! For real!

292
00:16:44,600 --> 00:16:47,188
You did so much for me
these past two years!

293
00:16:48,040 --> 00:16:50,760
No need to get sappy on me. Just go.

294
00:17:00,780 --> 00:17:02,000
One last thing!

295
00:17:04,180 --> 00:17:05,620
I'm gonna do it!

296
00:17:09,620 --> 00:17:11,260
I'm gonna be the king.

297
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:13,477
Of the pirates.

298
00:17:13,560 --> 00:17:14,840
You hear me?

299
00:17:26,980 --> 00:17:28,797
What are you doing?

300
00:17:28,880 --> 00:17:31,480
Hurry up and capture them already!

301
00:17:33,140 --> 00:17:34,537
Gotta move Luffy.

302
00:17:34,620 --> 00:17:36,800
We appreciate the help Rayleigh.

303
00:17:38,200 --> 00:17:40,177
Well, we're off.

304
00:17:40,260 --> 00:17:42,097
Thanks again for everything.

305
00:17:42,180 --> 00:17:43,140
See ya.

306
00:17:43,460 --> 00:17:44,540
I'm out of here.

307
00:17:49,400 --> 00:17:50,480
Good luck.

308
00:18:08,220 --> 00:18:09,620
They're on the move!

309
00:18:09,840 --> 00:18:10,780
After them!

310
00:18:10,960 --> 00:18:11,980
Let him get away!

311
00:18:14,260 --> 00:18:16,900
Let nothing stop you
from reaching the top!

312
00:18:19,440 --> 00:18:22,620
The Straw Hats are making
a beeline for Grove 42!

313
00:18:23,840 --> 00:18:25,740
Catch them at any cost!

314
00:18:33,400 --> 00:18:35,257
It's our King Barrel!

315
00:18:35,340 --> 00:18:37,780
Why don't you just let the boy sail?

316
00:18:38,040 --> 00:18:40,569
He's been out of the
game, so take it easy.

317
00:18:44,120 --> 00:18:45,520
That's an intense line.

318
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:49,765
If you think that's intense, then
why don't you try crossing it?

319
00:18:54,700 --> 00:18:56,120
Whoa! That's a lot!

320
00:18:56,340 --> 00:18:57,517
You really went all out!

321
00:18:57,600 --> 00:18:58,430
What's inside?

322
00:18:59,520 --> 00:19:00,800
It's our food stock!

323
00:19:01,080 --> 00:19:02,997
I bought in bulk because
I'm sure everyone's

324
00:19:03,080 --> 00:19:05,257
stomachs have gotten bigger
over these two years.

325
00:19:05,340 --> 00:19:07,677
This should keep us all happy for a while.

326
00:19:07,760 --> 00:19:08,590
Good thinking!

327
00:19:08,740 --> 00:19:11,057
They haven't had your
cooking in way too long!

328
00:19:11,140 --> 00:19:12,060
Over here!

329
00:19:12,300 --> 00:19:13,460
We found them!

330
00:19:14,840 --> 00:19:16,899
Crap, they get ahead of us somehow.

331
00:19:17,400 --> 00:19:19,677
Looks like we're gonna have
to fight our way through.

332
00:19:19,760 --> 00:19:20,590
Charge in!

333
00:19:20,673 --> 00:19:21,503
We got this!

334
00:19:26,840 --> 00:19:29,200
I'm as worthless as a flea.

335
00:19:29,680 --> 00:19:30,520
What's wrong?

336
00:19:30,780 --> 00:19:33,820
Get up before - I'll be a tick. Oh no!

337
00:19:34,500 --> 00:19:35,330
Ow!

338
00:19:35,413 --> 00:19:36,525
What happened to their morale?

339
00:19:42,980 --> 00:19:43,810
I...

340
00:19:43,893 --> 00:19:45,700
I'm nothing but a louse.

341
00:19:46,760 --> 00:19:48,231
This sure looks familiar.

342
00:19:51,380 --> 00:19:54,900
How did I know it was you
guys causing that ruckus?

343
00:19:57,260 --> 00:19:58,420
So typical.

344
00:19:59,700 --> 00:20:03,197
You're fooling around with the Navy
when you should have been gone long ago.

345
00:20:03,280 --> 00:20:04,110
Whoa!

346
00:20:04,460 --> 00:20:06,754
Well, aren't you a sight for sore eyes!

347
00:20:08,280 --> 00:20:09,540
Speak for yourself.

348
00:20:09,820 --> 00:20:11,897
If you were smart, you
would have bailed by now.

349
00:20:11,980 --> 00:20:15,797
You wouldn't even be here if it
weren't for me, so don't start, mister!

350
00:20:15,880 --> 00:20:18,939
Who knows where you would
have wound up on your own!

351
00:20:19,880 --> 00:20:22,115
The least you could do is be gracious!

352
00:20:23,620 --> 00:20:27,457
She's an actual woman with real-life
girly parts! Of course I am!

353
00:20:27,540 --> 00:20:29,257
What the hell is your damage, you freak!

354
00:20:29,340 --> 00:20:30,197
Alright, enough of this.

355
00:20:30,280 --> 00:20:31,197
You guys need to get moving.

356
00:20:31,280 --> 00:20:34,751
There's a Navy ships nearby,
so you're running out of time!

357
00:20:34,840 --> 00:20:38,075
If you don't get out of here
soon, you'll never escape!

358
00:20:43,140 --> 00:20:44,400
Look who's here!

359
00:20:45,860 --> 00:20:46,690
Usopp!

360
00:20:47,180 --> 00:20:48,010
Nami!

361
00:20:50,200 --> 00:20:51,030
Robin!

362
00:20:56,660 --> 00:20:57,490
Alright!

363
00:20:57,573 --> 00:20:58,403
You're here!

364
00:20:58,486 --> 00:20:59,316
What a surprise!

365
00:20:59,399 --> 00:21:01,016
I didn't think you'd abandon stardom!

366
00:21:01,340 --> 00:21:02,170
Attaboy!

367
00:21:03,700 --> 00:21:05,457
Nothing could keep me from coming back.

368
00:21:05,540 --> 00:21:06,893
I've missed you all so.

369
00:21:07,180 --> 00:21:10,827
I see that you two have only
grown lovelier in our time apart.

370
00:21:13,260 --> 00:21:16,720
With all that in mind, there's
something I need to know.

371
00:21:19,640 --> 00:21:21,287
It's already song time, huh?

372
00:21:25,580 --> 00:21:27,917
Please, Nami, may I look at your panties?

373
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:29,040
No way in hell!

374
00:21:29,500 --> 00:21:31,617
I never let you look
at them two years ago.

375
00:21:31,700 --> 00:21:32,957
Why would I let you see them now?

376
00:21:33,040 --> 00:21:35,160
I was just excited to see you.

377
00:21:35,420 --> 00:21:38,677
It made my soul shake, and
it's still shaking right now.

378
00:21:38,760 --> 00:21:40,757
In fact, it's about to leak out of my ear.

379
00:21:40,840 --> 00:21:44,297
I didn't think you could have a
muscle spasm without any muscles.

380
00:21:44,380 --> 00:21:45,210
Seriously?

381
00:21:45,300 --> 00:21:48,594
How is it none of you have
grown up after all this time?

382
00:21:50,240 --> 00:21:55,240
Rejection aside, I was actually expecting
to be the last one here. Don't worry.

383
00:21:55,460 --> 00:21:57,917
Chopper is off looking
for a missing companion.

384
00:21:58,000 --> 00:21:58,860
Huh? Hey!

385
00:22:05,800 --> 00:22:07,329
Talk about perfect timing!

386
00:22:08,980 --> 00:22:09,940
GUYS!

387
00:22:12,500 --> 00:22:13,330
Hey!

388
00:22:16,500 --> 00:22:18,029
Told you I would find him!

389
00:22:20,500 --> 00:22:22,760
Luffy! Zoro! ZACHI!

390
00:22:23,300 --> 00:22:24,130
Hey!

391
00:22:27,440 --> 00:22:28,660
Together again!

392
00:22:28,940 --> 00:22:30,764
I've been waiting for this day!

393
00:22:31,320 --> 00:22:33,100
And everyone looks stronger!

394
00:22:33,400 --> 00:22:34,360
I like it!

395
00:22:36,220 --> 00:22:38,240
It feels like it's been forever!

396
00:22:41,820 --> 00:22:43,617
Looks like we're the last...

397
00:22:43,700 --> 00:22:45,580
Hi, guys!

398
00:22:53,780 --> 00:22:54,610
Huh?

399
00:22:57,840 --> 00:22:58,800
He's everything!

400
00:23:06,280 --> 00:23:07,809
Thanks a lot for the ride.

401
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:10,941
Tell everyone back in the
birdie kingdom I say hi.

402
00:23:12,220 --> 00:23:13,140
How is he?

403
00:23:13,280 --> 00:23:14,717
Has the bleeding stopped yet?

404
00:23:14,800 --> 00:23:19,060
Not one, but two beautiful women
in front of me. Stay with me, man.

405
00:23:19,160 --> 00:23:20,219
Don't give up yet.

406
00:23:20,600 --> 00:23:21,737
It's no good, Chopper!

407
00:23:21,820 --> 00:23:23,761
He's getting paler by the second!

408
00:23:25,180 --> 00:23:27,860
You look so cool, Franky!

409
00:23:28,160 --> 00:23:29,800
Yeah, you think so? Good.

410
00:23:30,240 --> 00:23:33,946
But even if you didn't, I could
change my style at will, Mecca.

411
00:23:34,640 --> 00:23:35,470
Mecca!

412
00:23:36,120 --> 00:23:37,100
Okay, focus.

413
00:23:37,400 --> 00:23:39,576
This is no time to be fooling around.

414
00:23:39,720 --> 00:23:43,896
We need to get out of here while we
can before the Navy's on top of us.

415
00:23:45,960 --> 00:23:47,901
No, it looks like we're too late.

416
00:23:49,880 --> 00:23:51,520
I see three Navy ships.

417
00:23:55,660 --> 00:23:59,037
If we don't do something fast,
we're going to be dead in the water.

418
00:23:59,120 --> 00:23:59,950
Fire!

419
00:24:00,033 --> 00:24:01,147
Sink that ship at all costs!

420
00:24:06,800 --> 00:24:07,630
Slave...

421
00:24:07,713 --> 00:24:08,543
No!

422
00:24:13,460 --> 00:24:14,290
What?

423
00:24:14,373 --> 00:24:15,455
We stopped in midair.

424
00:24:16,060 --> 00:24:17,100
We... Captain.

425
00:24:20,200 --> 00:24:21,880
It's the Kuja Pirates!

426
00:24:24,780 --> 00:24:26,560
Answer me this, knaves.

427
00:24:27,740 --> 00:24:33,640
Which one of you had the audacity to
place your disgusting ship in my path?

428
00:24:41,860 --> 00:24:44,020
That flag, it can't be.

429
00:24:44,400 --> 00:24:45,260
You know it?

430
00:24:45,580 --> 00:24:46,933
That's the Kuja symbol.

431
00:24:47,080 --> 00:24:50,637
They're a strong crew of Amazonians
led by one of the Seven Warlords.

432
00:24:50,720 --> 00:24:51,737
You're joking, right?

433
00:24:51,820 --> 00:24:52,650
Not at all.

434
00:24:52,733 --> 00:24:53,677
Her name is Boa Hancock.

435
00:24:53,760 --> 00:24:56,737
They say anyone who lays eyes
on her will be enamored by

436
00:24:56,820 --> 00:24:59,537
her beauty and turned to stone
unless she grants you mercy.

437
00:24:59,620 --> 00:25:03,477
Oh, I can see why beauty
starts and ends with her.

438
00:25:03,560 --> 00:25:05,577
If I had eyes, they'd be sparkling.

439
00:25:05,660 --> 00:25:07,877
Wow, she's a real life goddess.

440
00:25:07,960 --> 00:25:11,617
Is she really that fine? Let me see.

441
00:25:11,700 --> 00:25:12,757
My goddess.

442
00:25:12,840 --> 00:25:14,637
Where gotta find her?

443
00:25:14,720 --> 00:25:16,637
I want to see. I wanna. I wanna.

444
00:25:16,720 --> 00:25:20,380
He's as hard as a rock.

445
00:25:21,080 --> 00:25:23,198
Hancock said she wasn't coming here.

446
00:25:24,080 --> 00:25:26,677
We order you to move
your ship out of the way.

447
00:25:26,760 --> 00:25:29,397
You're interfering with
official Navy business.

448
00:25:29,480 --> 00:25:31,362
It's your ship that's in my way.

449
00:25:31,520 --> 00:25:34,897
So I suppose it's you that's
interfering with official Navy business.

450
00:25:34,980 --> 00:25:37,280
Uh, that's really an immature argument.

451
00:25:37,520 --> 00:25:38,800
I get what I want.

452
00:25:40,480 --> 00:25:41,560
Go, Luffy.

453
00:25:42,020 --> 00:25:43,549
I've bought you some time.

454
00:25:45,220 --> 00:25:47,700
Circulus, I could die of ecstasy.

455
00:25:48,340 --> 00:25:49,677
Looks like we have an opening.

456
00:25:49,760 --> 00:25:50,720
Let's set sail.

457
00:25:50,880 --> 00:25:53,115
Do you know that warlord or something?

458
00:25:53,200 --> 00:25:54,030
Yeah.

459
00:25:54,113 --> 00:25:57,297
I made friends with her when that
bear guy sent me to Amazon Lily.

460
00:25:57,380 --> 00:25:59,977
You mean the legendary
island where only women live?

461
00:26:00,060 --> 00:26:02,236
I never believed it was a real place.

462
00:26:02,360 --> 00:26:05,357
You've been palling around
with the pirate empress?

463
00:26:05,440 --> 00:26:06,580
Come clean now!

464
00:26:06,800 --> 00:26:09,637
You weren't really training at all
these past two years, were you?

465
00:26:09,720 --> 00:26:11,017
What else would I have been doing?

466
00:26:11,100 --> 00:26:12,860
Damn, it's not fair.

467
00:26:13,080 --> 00:26:14,797
That would have been a dream come true.

468
00:26:14,880 --> 00:26:15,998
What's his problem?

469
00:26:17,200 --> 00:26:18,030
Wow.

470
00:26:18,113 --> 00:26:19,666
So those are Luffy's friends.

471
00:26:20,200 --> 00:26:23,397
I've never seen so many strange
creatures together before.

472
00:26:23,480 --> 00:26:24,310
There's one, two, three, four.

473
00:26:24,393 --> 00:26:26,204
They look like such a fun crew.

474
00:26:26,980 --> 00:26:29,580
Okay, everyone in position to set sail.

475
00:26:30,100 --> 00:26:31,300
Yes, there's one.

476
00:26:32,680 --> 00:26:34,151
What's the matter, Usopp?

477
00:26:34,820 --> 00:26:36,397
Something just occurred to me.

478
00:26:36,480 --> 00:26:38,917
You never said you beat
the Navy soldiers inland.

479
00:26:39,000 --> 00:26:39,830
We didn't.

480
00:26:39,913 --> 00:26:40,957
We just flew past them,

481
00:26:41,040 --> 00:26:43,897
but we could hear them shouting
from behind us in the distance.

482
00:26:43,980 --> 00:26:47,156
Then what could be stopping
them from coming after us?

483
00:26:55,060 --> 00:26:58,420
This is Backup Unit
Platoon 3. Do you copy?

484
00:26:59,840 --> 00:27:00,840
We read you.

485
00:27:01,040 --> 00:27:01,870
What's happening?

486
00:27:01,953 --> 00:27:04,060
We are unable to reach Grove 42.

487
00:27:04,620 --> 00:27:05,480
What? Why?

488
00:27:05,760 --> 00:27:10,300
Well, because there are giant bugs
currently halting our advance.

489
00:27:10,520 --> 00:27:11,540
Wait, giant what?

490
00:27:14,680 --> 00:27:16,360
These things are monsters.

491
00:27:20,260 --> 00:27:21,200
Shoot it!

492
00:27:28,660 --> 00:27:32,366
I won't let anyone get in the
way of Usoppun going adventuring.

493
00:27:35,780 --> 00:27:38,280
Men don't shed tears when they part ways.

494
00:27:40,020 --> 00:27:42,120
Good luck, Usoppun.

495
00:27:44,580 --> 00:27:46,820
Who cares why they're coming after us?

496
00:27:47,000 --> 00:27:49,677
The worse their lives are,
the better ours will be.

497
00:27:49,760 --> 00:27:51,760
Heh, it's time to get out of here.

498
00:27:52,100 --> 00:27:55,340
Nami, lead the way! You got it.

499
00:27:56,880 --> 00:27:57,710
Alright.

500
00:28:00,320 --> 00:28:01,940
This is Platoon 4.

501
00:28:02,140 --> 00:28:03,493
Afraid I have bad news.

502
00:28:03,760 --> 00:28:07,057
All our gunpowder has been
ruined by a sudden rain shower.

503
00:28:07,140 --> 00:28:07,970
What?

504
00:28:08,053 --> 00:28:09,080
That is impossible!

505
00:28:09,560 --> 00:28:14,000
The forecast for Sabaoni Archipelago
today is clear and sunny!

506
00:28:17,600 --> 00:28:19,360
Thunder would be excessive.

507
00:28:19,760 --> 00:28:22,657
After all, we don't want
to scare the civilians now.

508
00:28:22,740 --> 00:28:26,037
I wasn't expecting those bubbles
to give us so much grief.

509
00:28:26,120 --> 00:28:28,557
Bubbles or not, you can't
complain about the wind.

510
00:28:28,640 --> 00:28:29,470
No, sir.

511
00:28:29,553 --> 00:28:32,577
That breeze got us where we
wanted to be right on schedule.

512
00:28:32,660 --> 00:28:33,637
Of course it did.

513
00:28:33,720 --> 00:28:37,249
When it's something for Nami,
she gets nothing but the best.

514
00:28:40,160 --> 00:28:42,580
We'll miss you on Weatheria, young lady.

515
00:28:42,840 --> 00:28:45,134
But get out there and give it your all.

516
00:29:02,120 --> 00:29:03,820
Hey, what's it doing?

517
00:29:06,180 --> 00:29:08,592
Are you sure this is supposed to inflate?

518
00:29:11,680 --> 00:29:12,510
Whoa!

519
00:29:12,640 --> 00:29:14,581
Now our boat's got a bubble roof!

520
00:29:15,480 --> 00:29:16,757
This is how it works.

521
00:29:16,840 --> 00:29:19,277
A ship that is properly
coated has the ability

522
00:29:19,360 --> 00:29:21,317
to withstand almost any sort of pressure,

523
00:29:21,400 --> 00:29:23,397
but it also has very little buoyancy.

524
00:29:23,480 --> 00:29:26,837
The floating bag beneath the ship
is the only thing keeping us afloat.

525
00:29:26,920 --> 00:29:30,797
By deflating it, the sunny will
become less buoyant and begin to sink.

526
00:29:30,880 --> 00:29:32,468
It's pretty simple, really.

527
00:29:32,580 --> 00:29:33,700
Huh, interesting.

528
00:29:34,240 --> 00:29:35,497
Maybe not simple enough.

529
00:29:35,580 --> 00:29:36,617
Forget about it for now.

530
00:29:36,700 --> 00:29:37,637
Let's spread the sail.

531
00:29:37,720 --> 00:29:38,550
Why?

532
00:29:38,633 --> 00:29:40,397
We use it to catch the water current,

533
00:29:40,480 --> 00:29:42,797
similar to how we would use
the wind above sea level.

534
00:29:42,880 --> 00:29:45,397
I was hoping we'd just
sink down to fish man eye.

535
00:29:45,480 --> 00:29:46,310
Darn.

536
00:29:46,393 --> 00:29:47,223
All right!

537
00:29:47,306 --> 00:29:50,277
We'd better hurry unless we
want to get in another fight!

538
00:29:50,360 --> 00:29:53,220
This is Central Unit Platoon 5 at row 42.

539
00:29:53,800 --> 00:29:55,060
We have an emergency!

540
00:29:55,580 --> 00:29:57,457
The troops from Platoon 2 have been found,

541
00:29:57,540 --> 00:29:59,777
but they've all succumbed
to a severe depression!

542
00:29:59,860 --> 00:30:02,737
Tell him to suck it up
and get back in the fight!

543
00:30:02,820 --> 00:30:03,780
I suck!

544
00:30:03,960 --> 00:30:05,697
I should have been born a waterfall!

545
00:30:05,780 --> 00:30:09,997
What we've been able to gather is that
Straw Hat Luffy flew off on a giant bird!

546
00:30:10,080 --> 00:30:11,377
So he's not even there?

547
00:30:11,460 --> 00:30:13,077
Then what are you guys shooting at?

548
00:30:13,160 --> 00:30:16,042
We are currently under
attack by unknown enemies!

549
00:30:16,820 --> 00:30:18,697
The enforcement's got here quick.

550
00:30:18,780 --> 00:30:20,427
We were just about to leave.

551
00:30:20,940 --> 00:30:21,820
Heads up!

552
00:30:24,460 --> 00:30:27,040
The Straw Hat ship is now within range.

553
00:30:27,740 --> 00:30:29,340
But we may have a problem.

554
00:30:29,540 --> 00:30:31,893
A large bird is heading straight for us.

555
00:30:41,620 --> 00:30:42,480
Oh, wow!

556
00:30:43,960 --> 00:30:45,560
Uh, from behind, too?

557
00:30:45,960 --> 00:30:46,880
I got it!

558
00:30:49,440 --> 00:30:50,960
Like what you see, Nami?

559
00:30:51,160 --> 00:30:52,800
I've gotten a lot stronger.

560
00:30:53,360 --> 00:30:55,120
Go ahead and take it in.

561
00:30:55,940 --> 00:30:57,200
No, not again!

562
00:31:00,740 --> 00:31:02,060
Platoon 5, come in!

563
00:31:02,220 --> 00:31:03,161
What's going on?

564
00:31:03,420 --> 00:31:05,180
Well, it isn't good.

565
00:31:05,540 --> 00:31:06,893
We've hit interference.

566
00:31:07,120 --> 00:31:09,197
We couldn't possibly
have anticipated this.

567
00:31:09,280 --> 00:31:10,110
Ah!

568
00:31:10,193 --> 00:31:11,080
Have mercy!

569
00:31:13,760 --> 00:31:18,400
How could you ever think of turning
beauties like us away, as if?

570
00:31:18,620 --> 00:31:20,000
Maybe they're all shy.

571
00:31:20,600 --> 00:31:22,980
There's nothing to be ashamed of, boys.

572
00:31:23,840 --> 00:31:26,660
Let's have a cup of tea and cookies, too.

573
00:31:27,940 --> 00:31:28,770
How awful.

574
00:31:29,420 --> 00:31:31,302
Truly, this is worse than death.

575
00:31:34,040 --> 00:31:35,100
Hi there.

576
00:31:35,300 --> 00:31:37,241
You've got such an adorable face.

577
00:31:37,620 --> 00:31:39,480
No, let me go.

578
00:31:41,700 --> 00:31:42,940
What's wrong now?

579
00:31:43,160 --> 00:31:44,925
Platoon 5, finish your report!

580
00:31:46,260 --> 00:31:48,900
This is for you, Sanji. Make it count.

581
00:31:51,640 --> 00:31:52,470
Whoa!

582
00:31:52,553 --> 00:31:54,160
Take it easy, Sanji. Breathe!

583
00:31:55,060 --> 00:31:56,400
Usopp, it's you.

584
00:31:56,880 --> 00:32:00,645
Sorry, it felt like someone had
gotten a death grip on my heart.

585
00:32:00,780 --> 00:32:02,360
Bag's deflated! Awesome.

586
00:32:02,680 --> 00:32:03,760
You guys ready?

587
00:32:04,200 --> 00:32:05,540
Yeah, we're all set.

588
00:32:06,920 --> 00:32:08,096
That ain't it, Nami?

589
00:32:08,760 --> 00:32:09,590
Yeah.

590
00:32:09,673 --> 00:32:10,728
Just say the word, Captain.

591
00:32:17,600 --> 00:32:18,460
All right.

592
00:32:23,480 --> 00:32:24,740
Listen up, guys!

593
00:32:26,100 --> 00:32:28,917
There's a lot I want to say,
but we don't have much time.

594
00:32:29,000 --> 00:32:30,437
One thing can't wait, though.

595
00:32:30,520 --> 00:32:33,557
What you went through these past
two years was selfish of me,

596
00:32:33,640 --> 00:32:35,317
so thanks for putting up with it.

597
00:32:35,400 --> 00:32:37,957
You make it sound like this
has never happened before.

598
00:32:38,040 --> 00:32:38,980
That's no joke.

599
00:32:39,260 --> 00:32:41,789
You've always been a
selfish piece of work.

600
00:32:45,940 --> 00:32:48,880
Rear Admiral, the pirate
ship is submerging!

601
00:32:49,660 --> 00:32:50,660
You can't wait!

602
00:32:50,940 --> 00:32:54,293
Listen, you have no idea how
dangerous these pirates are!

603
00:32:54,580 --> 00:32:58,500
Move your ship now, pretty
please! Yes, please!

604
00:32:59,620 --> 00:33:02,340
Take care of yourself, Luffy.

605
00:33:05,320 --> 00:33:06,580
Spread yourself!

606
00:33:07,620 --> 00:33:08,450
Right!

607
00:33:15,800 --> 00:33:17,700
Let's go!

608
00:33:19,700 --> 00:33:20,530
Yeah!

609
00:33:27,300 --> 00:33:30,720
We're up to Fishman Island!

610
00:33:32,160 --> 00:33:33,620
We go!
